From b5fa42670f16aa290f9ed538e35f14e6fda4cf82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:04:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] intel_extreme: preserve Alder Lake clock-gating state

Do not apply the legacy i965 fallback to Alder Lake. Return unsupported before any writes until generation-specific gating exists. Other groups retain the inherited behavior. This is a safeguard, not GPU power management support.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex
Signed-off-by: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/intel_extreme/power.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/intel_extreme/power.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/intel_extreme/power.cpp
index 33eb8843..1564d8db 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/intel_extreme/power.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/intel_extreme/power.cpp
@@ -26,6 +26,11 @@ status_t
 intel_en_gating(intel_info &info)
 {
 	CALLED();
+	// The fallback below programs i965 registers, not Alder Lake clock gating.
+	// Preserve firmware state until generation-specific support is available.
+	if (info.device_type.InGroup(INTEL_GROUP_ALD))
+		return B_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+
 	// Fix some problems on certain chips (taken from X driver)
 	// TODO: clean this up
 	if (info.pci->device_id == 0x2a02 || info.pci->device_id == 0x2a12) {
-- 
2.43.0

